[#:seon.task{:id "132fee0467c8"
             :name "definitions-bypass-entry-gate"
             :kind :function
             :intent "Every definition an evaluation makes passes the entry gate and is armed, not only a top-level clojure.core/defn the reader matched: (do (defn …)), (let [..] (defn …)), (def f (fn …)) and defn-expanding macros must be refused when uncontracted. Keep an unindexed change distinct from an absent contract. A call inside the defining form still runs before the check."
             :must-read #{seon.sci.eval/evaluate seon.sci.eval/definition-row}
             :evidence #{"docs/research/agent-platform/language-requirements-2026-09-24.md"
                         "docs/prds/agent-platform/landing/lane-impl-task-slice2-2026-09-25.md"}}
 #:seon.task{:id "25cc3e2db48d"
             :name "requiring-a-dependency-is-refused"
             :kind :function
             :intent "(require '[malli.core :as m]) at an agent REPL is refused as an unindexed change naming all ~300 malli.core Vars ('This form changed malli.core/-->-schema ... which its analysis declares no definition for'), because the Vars load-host-namespace copies count as program definitions. Reproduced at HEAD 013e12924 as root (smoke 16:48Z) and on a fresh branch (16:55Z). The :load-fn of 2cae09887 is therefore unusable, (m/validate int? 1) stays unresolved, and agents still cannot validate a value. A dependency namespace's copied Vars are not program rows and must not be diffed as definitions."
             :must-read #{seon.sci.eval/copy-host-var seon.sci.eval/load-host-namespace seon.sci.eval/unindexed-change}
             :evidence #{"docs/research/agent-platform/landing/fix-agent-path-2026-09-26.md"
                         "docs/research/agent-platform/landing/task-log-2026-09-26.md"
                         "docs/research/agent-platform/landing/unrestrict-sci-2026-09-26.md"}}
 #:seon.task{:id "f548d10ecb69"
             :name "evaluate-declares-too-few-refusals"
             :kind :function
             :intent "seon.sci.eval/evaluate returns refusals its contract does not declare: the unindexed-change refusal (seen on every rejected require above) ends with 'Contract finding: seon.sci.eval/evaluate returned this error, and none of its declared error alternatives matches it.' Declare each refusal evaluate returns as its own named alternative."
             :must-read #{seon.sci.eval/evaluate seon.sci.eval/unindexed-change}
             :evidence #{"docs/research/agent-platform/agent-restrictions-and-rollback-2026-09-26.md"
                         "docs/research/agent-platform/landing/task-log-2026-09-26.md"}}
 #:seon.task{:id "a4f403e8c826"
             :name "in-ns-inside-do-is-refused"
             :kind :function
             :intent "(do (in-ns 'my.issue) (defn f ...)) is refused as an unindexed change ('This form changed my.issue/f, which its analysis declares no definition for'), because analysis attributes the do to the run's starting namespace. At clojure.main in-ns inside do works. Top-level in-ns then defn in one run already works. Still open in dogfood cycle 10 (#12)."
             :must-read #{seon.sci.eval/definition-row seon.sci.eval/unindexed-change}
             :evidence #{"docs/research/agent-platform/agent-restrictions-and-rollback-2026-09-26.md"
                         "docs/research/agent-platform/dogfood-report-2026-09-26.md"
                         "docs/seon/issues/dynamic-in-ns-cannot-persist-definition-namespace.md"}}
