 #:seon.task{:id "d653ed4b633f"
             :name "install-gate-interprets-file-tests-in-sci"
             :kind :function
             :intent "The install gate re-evaluates every reaching file test's source in the candidate's SCI (run-candidate-test!), where the test's own requires do not resolve: a docstring-only defn of my.note/add! gated 4 tests, 0 passed, each 'Unable to resolve symbol: support/with-database'; an arity change of my.fs/write! failed 3 of 3, while my.test/check ran the same 3 tests green in 7,165 ms. It also runs compiled host test bodies under an SCI arm that cannot interrupt them, which drove the 14:20Z recursion to 10.2 GB. Needs the owner's reach-executor ruling (loose-threads section 11 Q1: run unchanged file tests as compiled Vars with the branch definition bound, interpret only differing rows, or gate only branch tests and leave file tests to merge)."
             :must-read #{seon.sci.eval/evaluate-candidate seon.sci.eval/run-candidate-test! seon.turn/gate-function-install}
             :evidence #{"docs/research/agent-platform/dogfood-maintainer-opus-2026-09-26.md"
                         "docs/research/agent-platform/landing/fix-dogfood-api-2026-09-26.md"
                         "docs/research/agent-platform/landing/inv-heap-stuck-members-opus-2026-09-26.md"
                         "docs/seon/issues/a-first-party-redefinition-gates-on-saturated-reach-interpreted-in-sci-and-is-refused.md"}}
 #:seon.task{:id "fc812316b5da"
             :name "a-registration-lets-a-later-redefinition-skip-its-gate"
             :kind :function
             :intent "A breaking defn installs without its gate when a seon.schema/register! came earlier in the same run; the same defn alone is refused by its gating test (952 ms run). A bad normalize-tags with two gating tests installed the same way. A skipped gate and a passing gate both print #'ns/name. A gate that cannot run must refuse, never admit."
             :must-read #{seon.schema/register! seon.sci.eval/evaluate seon.turn/gate-function-install}
             :evidence #{"docs/research/agent-platform/dogfood-author-opus-2026-09-26.md"
                         "docs/seon/issues/a-schema-registration-earlier-in-a-run-lets-a-later-redefinition-install-ungated.md"}}
 #:seon.task{:id "85bb0e44a4b9"
             :name "a-contract-predicate-is-refused-both-ways"
             :kind :function
             :intent "A contract naming a predicate is refused both quoted and unquoted: [:=> [:cat] inst?] is refused because 'contracts are data; use ... a quoted symbol', and [:=> [:cat] 'inst?] is refused by canonical-definition as '(quote inst?)'. Two admission stages read two different values (evaluated metadata and authored source); only a registered schema key works."
             :must-read #{seon.schema/canonical-definition seon.sci.eval/definition-row}
             :evidence #{"docs/research/agent-platform/dogfood-author-opus-2026-09-26.md"
                         "docs/seon/issues/a-contract-predicate-is-refused-both-quoted-and-unquoted.md"}}
 #:seon.task{:id "c5f80919df38"
             :name "incremental-install-leaves-callers-on-the-jvm-definition"
             :kind :function
             :intent "install-row! installs an override's one row and does not interpret its affected callers, while regeneration (base-ctx on the changed database) does: with seon.id/valid? overridden, the affected closure has 11 members and regeneration binds 701 names incremental installation does not. Compiled callers direct-link the JVM definition, so after an incremental install they still call it, not the override."
             :must-read #{seon.sci.eval/base-ctx seon.sci.eval/install-row!}
             :evidence #{"docs/research/agent-platform/landing/fix-eval-schema-reds-2026-09-26.md"}}
 #:seon.task{:id "60fa86de1b8c"
             :name "repl-namespace-changes-drift-from-the-ns-text"
             :kind :function
             :intent "alias, refer and import at the REPL change a namespace row's facts but keep its stored ns text, so write-back's equivalence proof refuses :not-equivalent; a REPL-evaluated ns form also drops the row's :seon.fn/file. require was fixed (5ced0160b). Splice every namespace-table change into the stored ns form, and keep the file."
             :must-read #{seon.sci.eval/namespace-context-row seon.sci.eval/namespace-source}
             :evidence #{"docs/research/agent-platform/landing/merge-ns-rows-2026-09-26.md"
                         "docs/seon/issues/a-require-at-the-repl-records-the-require-form-as-its-namespaces-source.md"}}
 #:seon.task{:id "d215b1ebde7c"
             :name "acquisition-rebuilds-the-whole-program"
             :kind :function
             :intent "Acquiring a context re-derives the whole program: a base-ctx cache miss is 2,925 ms, dominated by acquire-program!; acquisition measured 1,467-3,376 ms; the first agent evaluation on a new branch allocated 11.2 GB and took 3.6 s JVM-wide; the base-context memo is keyed by program identity per commit, so every test-request commit misses (414-450 ms of the ~1 s clean-request-handle). The 16:10Z OOM died inside derive-base-ctx -> acquire-program! -> reverse-closure. Cost must follow the changed rows, not the program."
             :must-read #{seon.sci.eval/acquire! seon.sci.eval/acquire-program! seon.sci.eval/base-ctx seon.sci.eval/derive-base-ctx}
             :evidence #{"docs/research/agent-platform/landing/fix-test-request-cost-2026-09-26.md"
                         "docs/research/agent-platform/landing/inv-agent-run-stability-opus-2026-09-26.md"
                         "docs/research/agent-platform/landing/stability-guard-2026-09-26.md"
                         "docs/research/agent-platform/perf-profile-2026-09-26.md"}}
 #:seon.task{:id "07317379b8ae"
             :name "copied-vars-pin-old-wrapper-generations"
             :kind :function
             :intent "copy-host-var copies each JVM Var root into an sci.lang.Var, so a context alive across a reload pins a whole generation of instrument wrappers (2,070 of 2,072 old wrappers were held by one in-flight prepl evaluation, about 85 MB per generation). A copied dynamic Var's binding also never reaches the compiled library code that reads it. SCI can expose the clojure.lang.Var itself: reference instead of copy."
             :must-read #{seon.sci.eval/copy-host-var seon.sci.eval/load-host-namespace}
             :evidence #{"docs/research/agent-platform/landing/mem-idle-2026-09-26.md"
                         "docs/research/agent-platform/landing/unrestrict-sci-2026-09-26.md"}}
